    "summary": "Vessel (cooking pot) carved of out of one piece of soapstone (?), except for one of the long side walls, where a semi-circle formed piece is set in and bound through six pairs of holes with sinew (?). This semi-circular inset piece is broken in middle and mended. // Rectangular form, walls c 5-6 mm thick. // Carved projection (handle ?), 4.2 and 4.7 cm long respectively, in the middle of the outside of each of the short sides. // In all four upper corners drilled holes, where sinew (?) threads are attached to hang the cooking pot; threads are braided in upper part.",
